# Local development's own SQLite inspection history (services/storage.py's
# DB_PATH). Never bake this into the image: COPY happens before `USER
# appuser` in the Dockerfile, so any file here would land root-owned, and
# when a fresh named volume is first mounted over /app/data Docker's local
# volume driver copies the image directory's contents (including
# ownership) into it - silently making history writes fail with
# "attempt to write a readonly database" in every new deployment on any
# machine that ever ran the app locally first. Confirmed by direct
# container testing this session; data/.gitkeep (if present) still ships
# so the directory itself exists.
data/*.db
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite3
# Offline dataset/model-preparation tooling and experiment run outputs -
# never imported by the running application (app.py, models/, services/,
# utils/, pages/ have no `import training...`) but training/cloud/runs/
# alone can be 100+ MB of generated checkpoints/plots, needlessly bloating
# the build context and slowing every build.
training
*.patch
*.log
.DS_Store
